WEBVTT

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.710
Daichi?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.000
Time to get up.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.380
Gotcha...

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:42.890
Why do I feel like I was just having
a really important dream?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.060
It's no use. I can't remember.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.190
Now it's going to bother me all day.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:56.030
A Midsummer Night's
Dream

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.820
And summer break starts tomorrow...

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:03.410
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:10.590
I'm watching an endless dream

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:17.050
Aren't you watching too?

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:24.390
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:31.230
Can't you see it too?

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:36.650
The things you can't normally say

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.410
The things you try to express

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.910
The things you're willing to fight for

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:47.620
Standing on your own two feet

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:54.300
The night sky illuminates them all

00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:01.430
The first flash of lightning

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:07.770
This is our battle to fight

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:15.110
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:23.580
This dream will absolutely come true

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.960
I thought he quit the track team to focus on his studies...

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.050
Has he picked up any bad habits, like staying out late?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.010
No, nothing like that.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.720
There must be some sort of reason for his grades to be slipping like this.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.600
I was going to say that I'm pretty much always playing in my room,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.480
but I didn't.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.770
I didn't think it would help.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.900
I felt like I'd said it before.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.240
Wait... But when did I say that?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.030
Look, you need to put more thought toward what you're going to do after high school.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.290
Surely you have a dream you want to realize?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.660
Maybe you want to follow in your father's footsteps?

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.540
Sir...

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.210
Yes?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.960
His father has nothing to do with his future plans.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.300
Right now, I...

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.140
I think there might be something wrong with me. With the way I am.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.390
But you know, I'm probably just imagining it.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.520
Frankly, I'm just trying to escape school because I don't feel like studying

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.570
anything they assign there.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.070
Impressive, Daichi...

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.160
Huh? Amara!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.000
You're working?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.920
My family owns this place.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.210
Is it okay for me to come unannounced?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.420
Nah, it's fine. My parents aren't home.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:03.930
Come in.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.890
Oh, it's Daichi.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.970
I found him at the arcade.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.020
Oh? Moco and Ai?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.200
You're good at piloting robots, Daichi!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.660
R-Really?

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.750
Huh?

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.960
Piloting robots...

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:38.670
What was it?

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.420
Hey. We should invite Daichi too.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.880
And if we do, Ai will definitely come.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.350
Don't you think it would be better to have more people?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.350
You're right.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.680
Hey, a few of us are planning a trip to a summer house in Izu.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.100
You guys want to come along?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.020
A summer house?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.070
Is your four-eyed old man going to make a fuss?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.150
He isn't your real father though, right?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.200
How'd you know?

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.620
Daichi's father was an astronaut.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.250
I'm amazed you know that.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.120
I killed him!

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.170
What's wrong, Daichi?

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.000
N-Nothing!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.470
He <i>was</i> an astronaut?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.340
He's dead now.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.970
This footage was taken by a local resident.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.900
Hey, Daichi...

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.230
Come to Izu with me.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.200
Aren't you interested in this avatar's body?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.410
You'll come, won't you, Daichi?

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:54.910
I'll call you once the schedule's worked out.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.120
Let's enjoy summer vacation together.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.590
Okay, Daichi?

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.720
I wonder why it is...

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.890
The wind in this town feels strange.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:20.610
And the dream I had before I woke up this morning is really bothering me.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.020
But I just can't remember it.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:31.410
And now, an update on the strange light
that appeared over Tanegashima.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:38.960
Last night, at 11:20 PM, a strange light
was seen shining above Tanegashima.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.670
The weather bureau says it might
have been either a moonbow,

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.210
Hey, Daichi.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.920
a rainbow formed from lunar light,

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.300
Are you going home?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.130
Yeah.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.880
or a meteorological phenomenon
known as a circumhorizontal arc.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.880
Um...

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.590
Oh, Baku...

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.430
Are you really quitting the track team?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.220
Yeah.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.060
I already submitted the paperwork.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.020
That's a waste.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.600
Why are you quitting?

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.690
Why?

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.110
I don't know.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.070
Weren't you a candidate for the next captain?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.280
Why was I chosen?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.780
I see...

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.160
So that's what you didn't like.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.580
Hey, have you ever had a dream
you couldn't remember,

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.750
one that really bothered you?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.460
A dream?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.380
No, never mind.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.800
It's nothing.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.550
Dreams disappear the minute you wake up.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:35.970
Don't worry about it.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.890
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.810
Life is no different.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.610
Once you're dead, everything's over.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.820
It's been so long since we've
gone to a festival together.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.740
Festival?

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.040
Festival? What are they like?

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.130
Festival...

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.770
A festival, huh?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.170
What am I doing?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.960
Eyecatch

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.180
Comprehensive
Japaneses

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.180
— Modern —

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.570
You're going out?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.950
I'm going to the shrine.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.870
There's a festival today.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.290
Don't you have to study for your make-up tests?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.250
I promised someone.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.120
Promised?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.250
Actually, I didn't promise anyone.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.300
I just felt like I had to go.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.930
Don't stay out too late.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.260
Your teachers said to make sure you didn't
get into the habit of staying out late.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:42.310
By the way, Uncle...

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.060
Have I eaten any watermelon this year?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:47.940
Do you want to?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.900
No, that isn't it.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.400
I don't think you've had any yet this year.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.280
I guess not.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.110
I'll be back.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.790
What are these?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.580
These memories I've been recalling in flashes all day?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.670
Festival? What are they like?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.760
What kind of dream was it?

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:24.470
Excuse me...

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.230
Do you have some time now?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.060
What is it?

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.280
I'm a photographer for a men's fashion magazine.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.900
Are you interested in being a model?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.740
Huh?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.410
I'm so lucky to have run into someone like you!

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.830
You'll make a great model!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:47.410
How about it?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.160
Want to try it?

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.250
Um... I can't do that!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.880
Why not?

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.420
You won't know unless you try, right?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.470
A future you don't choose doesn't exist.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.350
Being a model's great...

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.680
The whole world becomes so much fun.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.680
I'm sorry.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.650
I've got somewhere to be today,
and I'm in a hurry.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.360
Really?

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.280
That's a shame.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.350
Um, if you'd like, you can use this.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:53.100
That's a very kind thing to do
for a girl you've never met.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.980
Is something wrong?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.070
I'm on my way to a funeral.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:01.280
For someone who was like family to me.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.910
Like family to you?

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.740
I was raised by someone who wasn't my parent.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.830
What a coincidence.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.380
But she wasn't really interested in me.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.340
She was only interested in my inheritance.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.970
She raised me to get her hands on it.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:25.430
And when I realized that,
I got mad and ran away.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:31.560
But she died in an accident.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.600
I still haven't forgiven her.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.110
But I'm still sad.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.740
You loved her.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.370
I don't know.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.160
But I use people to survive, as well.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.210
In that sense, I'm the same as she was.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.170
Don't people live by helping one another?

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:04.380
My way of life can't be masked
by such beautiful words.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.810
In the end, I'm living in a way I hate.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.730
And that makes my heart heavy.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.060
Then why not start by changing the way you live?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.690
If nothing else, that will make your heart lighter.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.450
Am I wrong?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.330
I don't think that's possible.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:37.370
You see, I'm the same as you.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.130
The same as me?

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.890
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.930
The bus has been involved in a minor collision.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.940
I apologize, but all passengers
are asked to disembark here.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.270
Maybe I was in too much of a rush.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.610
Are you okay?

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.610
I'm fine.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.830
After that, I'm amazed you're fine!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.540
Real humans don't die.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.210
Right, real princess?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.380
Let's go.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.970
You should go to a hospital, just in case.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.390
Oh, well. I guess I'll take a taxi or something.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.890
If you're going the same way, want to share?

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:41.400
No, I don't think I'm going
the same way as you yet.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.900
Goodbye.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.820
U-Um, my handkerchief...

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.250
The shrine in the third district, please.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.130
There was a bus accident, wasn't there?

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.960
You found out about that really quickly...

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.050
Do you get that kind of news on the taxi radio?

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.840
No, this was something different.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:18.560
I had a feeling there'd be a bus
accident in this area tonight.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.940
Like, intuition...

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:24.570
No, isn't that like a psychic power?

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.400
You've heard of déjà vu, haven't you?

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:33.280
When you visit a place for the first time,
but you feel you've been there before.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.790
I've had a really strong sense of that all day.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.580
Another coincidence...

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.580
And now, I even ended up predicting a bus accident.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.800
That's basically psychic power!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:51.680
Do you live in a country where
they believe in things like that?

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:53.220
A country?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.720
I'm surprised myself.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.140
What do you mean by
"a country where they believe"?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.060
I think it would be interesting

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:06.480
if you could relive a day with perfect
memories of what had happened.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.320
Would that be interesting?

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:14.910
If you knew what would happen,
you could do whatever you wanted.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.450
I think it would be boring to
just repeat the same thing...

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:24.120
I think it's more exciting not
knowing what will happen.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.130
Exciting, huh?

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.970
You don't feel frustrated, then?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.270
Thank you.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.560
Make sure you haven't forgotten anything,

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:47.230
Captain.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.990
Why did I decide I <i>had</i> to come here?

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:05.250
I still feel like I've forgotten something important.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.980
Please let the mission go well...

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.650
What "mission"?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.030
What have I forgotten?

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:24.410
I love the view of space from this planet most of all.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.460
So do I.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.260
What am I doing?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:43.430
Thanks.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.890
I have to go back.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.860
But how do I get back, exactly?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.280
How about a candy apple, sir?

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.240
Those look good!

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:03.700
But I'm sorry.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.040
I promised someone I'd eat one with them,

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.040
so not now.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.120
Oh?

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.750
Your girlfriend?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.170
Yeah.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.340
Now, then...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.760
What do I do?

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.520
I have to try that.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.270
Want to try it, sir?

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:36.980
How much for one go?

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.900
Three shots for two hundred yen! It's a bargain!

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.360
One go, then.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.120
So close!

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.080
But you have natural talent.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.620
Found you, Daichi!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:55.340
There you are, Daichi.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.750
The plan's have changed.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.510
We're leaving for that summer house tonight.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.550
Let's go, Daichi.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.760
Another close one!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.890
I've figured out the trick.

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:13.100
Real humans don't die.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.690
You guys keep saying that. What's a real human?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:20.030
Once you're dead, everything's over!

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.740
Is it?

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:26.240
The hopes my father left are still within me.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:29.700
A future you don't choose doesn't exist.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:32.830
That's why I'm going to choose one, of my own free will.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.540
Don't aim.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.630
Feel.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.960
Like the way you don't look at your right hand

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.090
and think, "This is my right hand."

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.180
Your right hand is a part of you,
so it's natural for it to be there.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.890
It isn't like it's "me and the gun."

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:55.690
It's like both of us comprise "me."

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.730
There's no time.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:58.570
Let's go, Daichi!

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.030
This shooting game doesn't matter!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:05.780
Let's go to that summer house and do something more fun.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.530
Sorry.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.280
I can't go to the summer house.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:15.620
There's something I have to do, no matter what.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:24.420
I don't think I'm going the same way as you yet.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.300
I'm going, though.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.600
I'm following the path I believe in.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:32.060
Aim carefully!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:52.740
Huh?

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.160
What was I just...

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.290
He's back.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.960
The captain is back.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:19.310
Good work, Captain.

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:21.060
You too, Akari.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.570
Are you okay, Captain?

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:25.440
I'm fine.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:26.440
No problem.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.450
I'm so glad...

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:30.200
Okay, everyone...

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:35.660
Let's go!

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:15.510
The hyperspace transport Entangle Link

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:19.720
carries our ship, <i>Blume</i>, away from Earth,
to a world unexplored by man.

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:24.520
But we landed somewhere other than our goal.

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:29.320
And a Kill-T-Gang appears there to destroy us.

00:24:29.320 --> 00:24:31.780
The Earth Engine is in terrible danger!

00:24:32.650 --> 00:24:35.660
Next time, on episode 24 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.160
Oberon

00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:37.160
<i>Oberon</i>.

00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:39.620
Earth Engine, expand!
